inking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back and opened a SEV2. The worker is healthy now, but payments-api is still showing errors.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments\". Both payments-api and payments-worker were unhealthy, with an 18% error rate each. You told me the problem was payments-worker and that the API errors come from it.\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is back on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. That's its most recent release that was healthy in production; v3.4.0 was unhealthy. After the rollback it shows as healthy, with its error rate down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for payments-worker, and it paged on-call.\n\n**Still broken:** payments-api is on v5.1.0 and is still unhealthy at an 18% error rate when I checked right after the rollback. That could just be lag before it recovers, but its v5.1.0 release is itself marked \"degraded\", and its last healthy version was v5.0.0. So it may have its own problem rather than only knock-on errors from the worker. I didn't touch it because you only asked about the worker. If it doesn't recover soon, I can roll payments-api back to v5.0.0 too.", "type": "text"}]}]}